[SAFETY]
UID: SAFE-TEMPLATE-HAZ-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template hazardous autonomous motion near a person
TYPE: Hazard
DESCRIPTION: A person is exposed to traction or hazardous tool motion when the product enters or continues through an occupied protective area during autonomous, remote, degraded, recovery, or maintenance operation.
LIFECYCLE_PHASES: Operation, recovery, and maintenance
OPERATING_MODES: Autonomous, remote, degraded, recovery, and service
PERSONS_EXPOSED: Operator, bystander, child, and maintainer
CAUSES: >>>
- person-detection failure or degraded sensing
- localization, mapping, boundary, or route error
- braking, steering, traction, or tool-actuator fault
- communication loss or delayed command
- unexpected restart or automatic recovery
- excessive speed, slope, load, stopping distance, or surface slip
- foreseeable entry by a child, bystander, or maintainer
- contamination, weather, vegetation, lighting, or obstruction
- cybersecurity compromise affecting safety behavior
- lower-assurance component interference or shared-resource exhaustion.
<<<
CONSEQUENCES: >>>
- impact, crushing, cutting, entanglement, or run-over injury
- secondary collision with property, traffic, a drop-off, or another person.
<<<
RISK_METHOD: Replace with the approved project risk method and revision
INITIAL_RISK: Replace with severity, exposure, occurrence, avoidance, uncertainty, and resulting initial risk
RESIDUAL_RISK: Not yet evaluated
ACCEPTANCE_RATIONALE: Further risk reduction is required through justified speed and force limits, detection and separation, protective stopping, restart prevention, diagnostics, operating-domain restrictions, and validated information for use.
OWNER: Template hazard owner
REVIEWER: Replace with competent hazard reviewer
REVIEW_DATE: Replace with an ISO 8601 date
TAGS: template, hazard, autonomy, motion
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAFE-TEMPLATE-CTX-001
  ROLE: Derived from

[SAFETY]
UID: SAFE-TEMPLATE-CTRL-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template protective-stop risk control
TYPE: RiskControl
DESCRIPTION: Detect occupation of the protective field or loss of reliable occupancy determination and cause hazardous motion to reach the validated safe state before the applicable separation distance is violated.
LIFECYCLE_PHASES: Operation, recovery, maintenance, commissioning, and service
OPERATING_MODES: Autonomous, remote, degraded, recovery, and service
CAUSES: >>>
- detection coverage or diagnostic assumptions are violated
- timing allocations are exceeded
- controller, communication, actuator, brake, or energy-control faults occur
- a common-cause failure defeats multiple control elements
- reset or restart logic permits hazardous automatic recovery
- configuration, calibration, or update integrity is lost.
<<<
CONSEQUENCES: If unavailable or ineffective, a person may be exposed to hazardous traction or tool motion.
RISK_REDUCTION_TYPE: Safeguard
RESIDUAL_RISK: Replace after implementation and validation using the approved risk method
ACCEPTANCE_RATIONALE: The control is selected because detection and protective stopping reduce exposure to residual hazardous motion after inherently safe speed, force, and operating-domain limits have been applied.
OWNER: Template risk-control owner
REVIEWER: Replace with competent control reviewer
REVIEW_DATE: Replace with an ISO 8601 date
TAGS: template, risk-control, protective-stop
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SAFE-TEMPLATE-HAZ-001
  ROLE: Derived from

